      },
      "text": "The stem is the plant's scaffold and distribution system — conducting water and sugar between root and leaf, and in woody plants, accumulating structural support that makes century-spanning growth possible. The transition from herbaceous to woody growth involves a lateral meristem (cambium) that is absent in grasses but present in all trees."
    },
